---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { seo } from "../config/seo";

// Bump whenever the policy text changes
const updated = new Date("2026-10-24T12:00:00");
const updatedLabel = updated.toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
  year: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  day: "numeric",
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Revealing Truth Church handles the information you share through our website, online giving and when you contact us."
>
  <main>
    {/* Dark band: the site header overlays the top of every page and its
        logo and menu toggle are drawn for a dark backdrop */}
    <header class="policy-head section" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="policy wrapper flow" data-width="narrow">
        <h1 class="font-display text-high-contrast">
          Privacy <span class="font-accent text-brand">policy</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="policy__updated">
          Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}
            >{updatedLabel}</time
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <article class="policy wrapper flow section" data-width="narrow">
      <p>
        Revealing Truth Ministries (“Revealing Truth Church,” “we,” “us”)
        respects your privacy. This policy explains what information we collect
        through revealingtruth.org, how we use it, and the choices you have. We
        keep it short because we collect very little.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can browse this website without giving us any personal information.</li>
        <li>We don’t use advertising trackers, analytics cookies or marketing pixels.</li>
        <li>We never sell, rent or trade your information.</li>
        <li>Online giving is handled by Pushpay. We never see your card or bank details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
      <p>
        Like every website, our hosting provider, Cloudflare, receives basic
        technical information each time a page loads: your IP address, browser
        and device type, the page requested and the time of the request. This
        is used to deliver the site, keep it secure and fix errors. These logs
        are kept for a short period and are not used to identify you.
      </p>

      <h3>When you give online</h3>
      <p>
        Our Give button takes you to Pushpay, a payment provider built for
        churches. Pushpay collects your payment details directly and processes
        them under its own
        <a href="https://pushpay.com/legal-center/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
        We receive your name, contact details and gift history so we can
        process your gift, send giving statements for tax purposes and answer
        questions about your giving. We do not receive or store your card or
        bank account numbers.
      </p>

      <h3>When you contact us</h3>
      <p>
        If you call, write or talk with us, we keep the information you choose
        to share, such as your name, phone number, email address or a prayer
        request, so we can respond and care for you. Prayer requests are shared
        only with the pastors and prayer team who need them, and never posted
        publicly without your permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set cookies of its own. Cloudflare may set a
        strictly necessary security cookie to tell people apart from automated
        bot traffic. It contains no personal information and is not used for
        advertising. Our fonts are hosted on our own site, so loading a page
        does not send your information to font services.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>We share information only with services that help us run the church:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website and its videos
          (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pushpay</strong> processes online gifts
          (<a href="https://pushpay.com/legal-center/privacy/">privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect
        the safety of someone in our church community.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to our YouTube, Instagram and Facebook pages take you to those
        services, where their own privacy policies apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is not directed at children under 13, and we do not
        knowingly collect personal information from them online. Information
        for Creative Kids and student ministries comes from parents or
        guardians. If you believe a child has sent us personal information,
        contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>
        We keep giving records as long as the law requires for tax and
        accounting purposes. Other information is kept only as long as we need
        it to serve you, then deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
      <p>
        This site is served only over an encrypted connection (HTTPS), and we
        limit access to personal information to staff and volunteers who need
        it. No system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable care to
        protect what you share with us.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us at any time to see, correct or delete the information we
        hold about you, or to stop contacting you. We will respond within 30
        days. Giving records we are required by law to keep can’t be deleted,
        but we will not use them for anything else.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle information, for example by adding a sign-up
        form, we will update this page and the date at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <address>
        Revealing Truth Ministries<br />
        5201 N. Armenia Ave, Tampa, FL 33603<br />
        <a href={`tel:${seo.telephone}`}>813-354-1135</a>
      </address>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    --flow-space: var(--size-400);
    max-inline-size: 45rem;
  }

  /* Clears the absolutely positioned site header */
  .policy-head {
    padding-block-start: calc(var(--section-padding) + 5rem);
  }

  .policy h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-heading-lg);
  }

  .policy__updated {
    font-family: var(--ff-ui);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  .policy h2 {
    --flow-space: var(--size-700);
    font-family: var(--ff-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-heading-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semi-bold);
    line-height: var(--lh-heading);
    color: var(--text-high-contrast);
  }

  .policy h3 {
    --flow-space: var(--size-500);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semi-bold);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .policy ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25em;
  }

  .policy li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--size-200);
  }

  .policy strong {
    font-weight: var(--fw-semi-bold);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .policy address {
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    text-decoration-color: var(--text-brand);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .policy a:hover {
    color: var(--text-brand);
  }

  .policy a:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--border-width-2) solid var(--focus-ring);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
